\title{LFCS 40}
\author{liamoc}
\date{2026-09-09}
\p{We had a celebration of 40 years since the foundation of the Laboratory for Foundations of Computer Science (LFCS) by [[milner]], [[burstall]] and [[plotkin]] today. This was the institute that I was (and in some sense, remain) part of at the [[uoe]]. I don't have much time for navel-gazing, and sadly most of the technical talks were either well outside my area, a demonstration of how brain-poisoned by LLMs my former Edinburgh colleagues have become, or both. I didn't really get much out of the day.}
\p{I am still glad to be here in Edinburgh for this week, though. It's great to catch up with some old friends.}